ition (Column 1) connected to an owned corner (A1) is a fundamental strategy. It secures territory that is difficult for the opponent to recapture.\n2.  **Mobility Strategy**: It is a "quiet move," flipping only a single opponent piece (C2). By minimizing the number of flipped pieces, I limit the number of new legal moves created for the opponent, restricting their options.\n3.  **Connection**: It strengthens the group around the A1 corner without opening up the board recklessly like moves (F, 4) or (E, 6) would.\n\nAnswer: (D, 1)'}
