ck the strategic weight of a corner.\n\nReason: (H, 8) is a corner position. In Reversi, corners are the most valuable squares because pieces placed there are stable and can never be flipped by the opponent. Taking this corner secures the bottom-right sector of the board, flips a diagonal line of opponent pieces (G7, F6, E5), and restricts the opponent's future mobility.\n\nAnswer: (H, 8)"}
